In article <1990Sep13.101214.27394@midway.uchicago.edu> rei3@ellis.uchicago.edu (ted reichardt) writes:
>	I've noticed this, too.  Sometimes warning seems to do nothing
>for a long time, then it'll kick in again.  Perhaps it only warns if
>you have not detected the monster in question even via telepathy
>before?

No, it's supposed to happen all the time.  It also depends on your level; the
monster's level must be above yours.

>>12. I dipped some scrolls in a fountain, figuring I'd roll my own with my
>>magic (tm) marker (46).  Alas, when I went to write, it said, "In your
>>haste, you rip the scroll to shreds".  I tried again, this time waiting
>>what I thought was quite a long time, and it still tore the scroll.  Do you
>>need fire or something to dry the scrolls, or do you just have to wait a
>>very long time?
>	Probably your marker is cursed.

No, scrolls must be identified before you can write on them.  This is to
keep people from just trying their magic marker out on every scroll they find
in order to see which ones are blank.

Tearing the scroll is, admittedly, a bit silly....
